      {
         "id": "SECTION_language",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### A Symbol for Equality\n\nTo say that something is equal, we use the symbol \"=\". For example, to say that two numbers are equal, we write:",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<center><span class=\"text_to_paint\">0</span> <span class=\"text_to_paint\">=</span> <span class=\"text_to_paint\">0</span></center>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "An important detail about equality: once it is established, it must be maintained. This means that when we change one side, the other side must be changed in the same way. Let us try an exercise with numbers and our hands, using arrows to illustrate:",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><table id=\"yupana0\" class=\"tawapukllay\"><tr><th colspan=\"4\"><i>Equation</i></th><th>Left Hand</th><th>Right Hand</th><th>Arrows</th></tr> <tr id=\"tf1\"><td id=\"tc1f1\"><span class=\"text_to_paint\" id=\"leftnum\">0</span></td> <td id=\"tc2f1\" colspan=\"2\"><span class=\"text_to_paint\">=</span></td> <td id=\"tc4f1\"><span class=\"text_to_paint\" id=\"rightnum\">0</span></td><td id=\"tc5f1\" style=\"background-color:white;\"><img id=\"leftHandImg\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('leftHandImg', '0%')\"  /></td><td id=\"tc6f1\"><img id=\"rightHandImg\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('rightHandImg', '0%')\"  /></td><td id=\"tc7f1\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-caret-up upArrowWithFA\" id=\"traineeUp0\"></i>  <i class=\"fa-solid fa-caret-down downArrowWithFA\" style=\"font-size:4em;color:#00f;\" id=\"traineeDown0\"></i></td></tr></table><p class=\"desc\"><b>Table 1</b>: Maintaining equality.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_conclusion",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Conclusion\n\nIn this text, we explored the concept of equality.\n\nWe also learned that objects can be exactly equal in every aspect, or they can be similar — sharing many characteristics but differing in a few.\n\nFinally, we saw how mathematical language allows us to express complex comparisons in a simple and precise way.\n\nIn the next text, we will dive deeper into the different degrees of equality and how they apply in various fields of knowledge.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      }
